            sample: "A student could apply selecting the strongest scenes by keeping the essay focused on one arguable line of interpretation. Choosing the strongest scenes, such as Jo refusing Laurie or Beth's illness, is more effective than mentioning every event. Selectivity allows deeper analysis and better control of time. Used well, it shows that quality of evidence matters more than quantity.",
