            sample: "Strong responses will argue that Alcott uses absence and return to structure the family's emotional journey. A clear structure might begin with Letters from Father sustain the girls during his absence, and his Christmas homecoming closes Part 1. It could then connect this to the sisters play at being pilgrims, and part 1 repeatedly echoes bunyan's pilgrim's progress. to show how the novel develops the idea that childhood play can become a language for ethical development. A final section could consider beth contracts scarlet fever after caring for the hummels and never fully recovers. and judge how these details together support the claim that Alcott gives moral choices real physical consequences. Reward close reference to scenes, accurate discussion of language and sustained evaluation.",
