            sample: "Strong responses will argue that The structure itself dramatises the movement from innocence to experience. A clear structure might begin with The novel moves from the girls' adolescence in Part 1 to adult decisions and losses in Part 2. It could then connect this to jo leaves home for a new york boarding house, where she writes for money and meets friedrich bhaer. to show how the novel develops the idea that leaving home can sharpen rather than erase moral identity. A final section could consider little women draws closely on louisa may alcott's own family life in concord, massachusetts. and judge how these details together support the claim that Alcott turns autobiographical material into a persuasive portrait of family life. Reward close reference to scenes, accurate discussion of language and sustained evaluation.",
