            q: "Critical essay (15 marks): Evaluate how Alcott uses Jo's move to New York to connect personal experience with broader values.",
            sample: "Strong responses will argue that Alcott uses a temporary city setting to widen Jo's horizons without abandoning the novel's ethical focus. A clear structure might begin with Jo leaves home for a New York boarding house, where she writes for money and meets Friedrich Bhaer. It could then connect this to little women draws closely on louisa may alcott's own family life in concord, massachusetts. to show how the novel develops the idea that ordinary domestic experience can carry serious literary and emotional weight. A final section could consider the novel opens while father is serving as a union chaplain during the american civil war. and judge how these details together support the claim that Alcott places the March home inside a recognisable wartime context rather than a timeless fairy-tale world. Reward close reference to scenes, accurate discussion of language and sustained evaluation.",
            marks: 15
