            q: "Critical essay (10 marks): To what extent is Jo March central to the novel as a whole?",
            sample: "Strong responses will argue that Jo makes Little Women more than a simple domestic novel. A clear structure might begin with Jo is the impulsive, ambitious writer whose fierce independence drives much of the novel's action. It could then connect this to beth is shy, musical and devoted to home, becoming the novel's quiet moral centre. to show how the novel develops the idea that quiet goodness can reshape a household. A final section could consider amy begins as vain and socially conscious but grows into a disciplined, self-aware young woman. and judge how these details together support the claim that Amy's arc rewards self-knowledge, not mere prettiness. Reward close reference to scenes, accurate discussion of language and sustained evaluation.",
